    "turn_text": "Yeah, and one of the key things that Democrats have put forward but is missing from the Republican side is any action on qualified immunity. So that's that legal doctrine that has often shielded police officers from civil lawsuits over misconduct on the job. On Monday, as we mentioned, the Supreme Court declined to hear cases challenging this legal immunity for police officers, leaving the issue up to lawmakers. But it's become an early sticking point between both parties.",
