    "turn_text": "Let's wrap up with some headlines. Violent clashes along China and India's border left 20 Indian soldiers dead on Tuesday. It's the first deadly confrontation to happen there in over 70 years. In the past few weeks, both countries have been sending more and more troops to that border, which has historically been a very disputed area. The unmarked territory plus lots of military presence equals major tensions, and there have reportedly been shouting matches, stone throwing, and even one cross-border fistfight.",
